# Mimir's own .mimirignore.
#
# This repo is a secret scanner, so it is full of deliberately fake credentials:
# test fixtures, rule regexes, and planning docs that quote example tokens. They
# are not leaks, and they would otherwise make `mimir scan .` fail on its own
# source tree — which is what the CI self-scan job runs.
#
# It also serves as a worked example of the format: one glob per line, `#` for
# comments, and a leading `!` to re-include a path.

# Fixture repos carrying intentionally-planted secrets.
testdata/**

# Fuzz corpora: seeds and saved crashers are, by construction, strings that
# look like credentials. They live under a testdata/ dir inside each package,
# so they need their own glob rather than the root testdata/** above.
**/testdata/fuzz/**

# Test files embed fake tokens as inputs and expectations.
**/*_test.go

# The default ruleset quotes token prefixes inside its own regexes.
config/mimir.toml

# Planning/spec docs quote example tokens in prose.
.planning/**
.gsd/**
.claude/**

# Tool config that names secret-ish patterns.
.semgrepignore
